{
  "version": 1,
  "name": "called",
  "about": "Her host asks this end to do one thing for her (call.ask). The child acks it, and what is not its to do it answers itself, at once, without the shell: an action it did not offer (call_unknown), another version (version_unsupported, saying the one it does), someone the action is not for (wrong_audience), one her host has said is not granted now (call_not_granted), a deadline already past (call_timeout). The rest it hands to the shell once, and sends the shell's one answer as a reliable call.result whose id is the call's and .result. Asked again while the call is in hand it only acks; asked again once answered it answers the same; either way it does nothing again. A result the contract does not take is told to the shell and answered internal_error. A deadline that passes while the shell is at it stops the call and answers call_timeout; what the shell says of that call afterwards is not sent.",
  "capabilities": ["calls"],
